# EKS Study Notes — Quick Reference

---

## Core Concepts (One Line Each)

| Term | What it is |
|------|-----------|
| **EKS** | AWS-managed Kubernetes — AWS runs the control plane, you manage the apps |
| **Node** | EC2 server where your pods actually run |
| **Pod** | One running copy of your container/app |
| **Deployment** | "Keep N copies of my pod alive always" |
| **Service** | Stable internal address to reach your pods |
| **Ingress** | Single entry point that routes traffic to many services |
| **Helm** | Package manager for Kubernetes — like apt/brew but for K8s |
| **IRSA** | Gives pods a secure AWS identity without hardcoded keys |
| **Karpenter** | Auto-adds/removes EC2 nodes based on pod demand |
| **ECR** | AWS private Docker image registry |
| **OIDC** | The bridge that connects Kubernetes service accounts to AWS IAM |

